course: dictionary
lesson: 4814
title: A hundred and hundreds of
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hundred is the number 100. It is ten tens, so if you count out ten groups of ten, you have a hundred. You write it as 100, with a 1 and two zeros.
explain: Hundreds also means a large number when you do not need an exact count. «Loot boxes work like gambling, and some children have spent hundreds without their parents knowing.» Hundreds here does not mean exactly 200 or 500. It means a lot of money, too much to count.
explain: In a whole number, the hundreds place is the third digit from the right. In 352, the hundreds digit is 3. Context helps again: «hundreds of stars» means a huge number of stars, not a set of 100.
fact: A hundred is 100, which is ten tens.
fact: Hundreds means many, a large number with no exact count.
fact: The hundreds place is the third digit from the right in a whole number: in 407, the hundreds digit is 4.
fact: «A hundred per cent» means all of something, or completely.
fact: 100 years make a century: «the 1st century was years 1 to 100».
exercise: «Loot boxes work like gambling, and some children have spent hundreds without their parents knowing.» What does hundreds mean here? | *A large number, with no exact count | Exactly 1000 | Exactly 100 | Exactly 10
exercise: In the number 437, which digit is in the hundreds place? | *4 | 7 | 3 | 37
exercise: How many tens make a hundred? | *10 | 100 | 5 | 20
test: «The 1st century was years 1 to 100.» How many years is that? | 10 | *100 | 50 | 1000
test: What is the hundreds digit of 829? | 82 | 9 | *8 | 2
exam: «About five hundred years ago», how is five hundred written in figures? | 50 | 15 | *500 | 5000
